": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about places in a limited range of social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "after", "type": "name"}, {"content": "when a time has happened", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(preposition) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Please check in after 12 p.m.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when traveling. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Western ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "coming from Europe and North America", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can have a Western breakfast.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Chinese", "type": "name"}, {"content": "relating to China", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You could have a Chinese breakfast as well.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "combination ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "two or more different things that can be put together", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We also offer a combination breakfast.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to depart", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to leave", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  The bus departs from the hotel at 9 a.m.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to cover", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to include", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  The tour covers The Great Wall of China and the Forbidden City. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn4le16ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Talking About Intentions and Plans", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> and <span class=\"strong\">be going to</span> to talk about future actions and events. <br/><br/>    You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> to talk about arrangements and plans. <span class=\"strong\">Be going to</span> puts an emphasis on the idea of intention (you decide to do something). <br/>    Examples: <br><span class=\"italic\"> <ul><li>We are departing from the hotel at 9 a.m.</span></li><li><span class=\"italic\">We are going to return around 5 p.m.</span></li> <li>The bus is leaving in 10 minutes. </li>    <li> We're traveling to Beijing next week. These are the tickets. </li>     <li>I'm going to visit Paris next year.</li>      <li>He's going to visit all the museums and monuments.</li></ul><br/></span>   You can use <span class=\"strong\">intend to</span> in place of <span class=\"strong\">be going to</span>. <br/>   Example: <span class=\"italic\">I intend to arrive early.</span><br><br>Remember that you need to conjugate the auxiliary verb TO BE for both the Present Continuous and be going to.", "type": "describer"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go on the Internet.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Research a tour you can take in Beijing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make sure you research the tour in English.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Answer these questions: <ul><li>How many days is it?</li> <li> What places do you go to?</li> <li>What things do you do?</li> <li>What transportation do you use?</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Share your answers with your class.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research about an overseas tour.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I locate specific information to answer questions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I communicate my information to a group.", "type": "text"}]}]}